// The browser suite's typechecker.
//
// Playwright transpiles a spec with esbuild, which strips types without
// checking them, so a spec is not typechecked by running it: only a *syntax*
// error stops the run. Nor is it typechecked by `tsconfig.json`, whose
// `include` is the application, or by vitest, whose include is
// `src/**/*.test.ts`. Without this file the specs are checked by nothing at
// all: a `page.getByRole("buton")` compiles, runs, and fails at whatever the
// locator eventually times out on rather than at the typo.
//
// It is a second project rather than three more globs in `tsconfig.json`
// because the two need different ambient types and cannot share one. The
// application is checked with `types: ["vitest/globals"]`, which keeps Node's
// globals out of code that runs in a browser. `playwright-core`'s own
// `types.d.ts` is written against them (`Buffer`, `fs`, `stream`,
// `Symbol.asyncDispose`) and produces about sixty errors of its own under
// that setting. Everything else, `strict` and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`
// included, is inherited so the specs are held to the application's standard.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["node"],
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["tests/browser/**/*.ts", "playwright.config.ts"]
}
